466	  <section class="hero">
467	    <div class="hero-texture" aria-hidden="true"></div>
468	    <span class="eyebrow">Engineer &amp; Researcher</span>
469	    <h1>I build technology and evidence for a world that does not require sight to move through it.</h1>
470	    <p class="lede">
471	      A blind tester in Herat once called an early prototype "my magical friend." That sentence has shaped
472	      every version I have built since. My work moves between hardware, research, and a nonprofit built to
473	      carry both further than I can alone.
474	    </p>
475	    <div class="cta">
476	      <a href="mailto:saidms@teww.org" class="primary">Get in touch</a>
477	      <a href="https://teww.org">Third Eye Worldwide</a>
478	    </div>
479	    <span class="status-line">Project Owner, CEAL, Columbia University</span>
480	  </section>
481	
482	  <section class="entry" id="recent">
483	    <span class="index-mark">01</span>
484	    <span class="tag">Recent</span>
485	    <h2>Recent Activity</h2>
486	    <ul class="recent-list">
487	      <li class="recent-item">
488	        <div class="recent-main">
489	          <span class="recent-title">Project Owner, CEAL</span>
490	          <span class="recent-detail">Computer Enabled Abilities Lab, Columbia University, with Professor Brian Smith</span>
491	        </div>
492	        <span class="recent-year">2026</span>
493	      </li>
494	      <li class="recent-item">
495	        <div class="recent-main">
496	          <span class="recent-title">Research in Progress</span>
497	          <span class="recent-detail">Four ongoing papers and design documents, from Third Eye Kit v2 to Third Eye Language</span>
498	        </div>
499	        <span class="recent-year">2025 &ndash;</span>
500	      </li>
501	      <li class="recent-item">
502	        <div class="recent-main">
503	          <span class="recent-title">Semiconductor Manufacturing Specialist</span>
504	          <span class="recent-detail">Intel Corporation, Hillsboro, Oregon</span>
505	        </div>
506	        <span class="recent-year">2025 &ndash;</span>
507	      </li>
508	    </ul>
509	
510	    <button class="excerpt-toggle" id="cealToggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cealBlock">
511	      More about CEAL
512	    </button>
513	    <div class="ceal-detail" id="cealBlock" hidden>
514	      <p>
515	        What has stayed with me since joining is how the lab sees the blind community as fully capable,
516	        not only in navigation and mobility, but in games, in art, and the full range of what people enjoy.
517	        It is a bigger vision than I was used to seeing.
518	      </p>
519	      <p>
520	        Every member of the lab carries the same underlying quality, intentional care. It does not happen
521	        by accident. It comes from how the lab is led and the space given to each person to do their own
522	        work. My first meeting with the team was scheduled earlier than usual so a member who was in China
523	        at the time could join. No one announced it. Everyone simply shifted their own schedule. That quiet
524	        decision told me more about the lab than any mission statement could, and it made me feel at home
525	        before I had really started.
526	      </p>
527	    </div>
528	  </section>
529	
530	  <section class="entry" id="teww">
531	    <span class="index-mark">02</span>
532	    <span class="tag">Organization</span>
533	    <h2>Third Eye Worldwide</h2>
534	    <p>
535	      One device was never going to be enough. Third Eye Worldwide is the organization I founded to carry
536	      that work further, a nonprofit building technology, community, and advocacy resources for blind and
537	      low-vision people globally. It is the reason Third Eye Kit and Heard exist as an ongoing body of
538	      work rather than a single finished project.
539	    </p>
540	    <p>
541	      I am committed to leading Third Eye Worldwide toward becoming a true global home for visually
542	      impaired people, a place where they find inclusion, independence, and education. It is where hearts
543	      get warmer, and where we learn to see and hear each other. I welcome collaboration on this journey.
544	    </p>
545	    <a class="link-out" href="https://teww.org">teww.org</a>
546	  </section>
